Indigo needs php (version 8 required), php-xml, and, for the gallery 
example, php-gd. 

The documentation needs geshi-1.0 and parsedown to work. Instructions
on how to install them are contained in the 'contrib' directory
and will also appear in your browser.

Some directories need to be writable by the web server so that php
can create files in them. On most systems it should be sufficient 
to change ownership to 'www-data'. They are:

docs/cache
resources/gallery/thumbnails

You will be alerted to wrong permissions in your browser window as well.

Otherwise there is no further installation required.
